course: dictionary
lesson: 16115
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Whacked is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask: what would make sense here? «He whacked the ball over the fence.» The ball is being hit, so whacked means hit hard.
explain: Now read this: «After the long day at school, I'm whacked.» Nobody is being hit here. Whacked means extremely tired. The words «long day» are the clue.
explain: Slang can change a word's meaning too. In US slang, «That idea is whacked» means that idea is crazy or strange. Look at the whole sentence and the people speaking to find the meaning that fits.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Whacked» means hit hard with a loud noise, as in «he whacked the ball».
fact: In British and Australian talk, «whacked» or «whacked out» means extremely tired, as in «I'm whacked».
fact: In US slang, «whacked» or «wacked» can mean crazy or strange.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «He whacked the ball over the fence.» What does whacked mean here? | Tired after a long day | *Hit hard with a loud noise | Crazy or strange
exercise: «After the long football match, I'm whacked.» What does whacked mean? | Crazy or strange | Wet through | Hit hard | *Extremely tired
exercise: Sam says, «That idea is whacked!» In US slang, what does whacked mean? | Hit very hard | *Crazy or strange | Very tired | Brand new
test: «The wind whacked the door shut.» Which meaning fits best? | *Hit with a loud bang | Happy and smiling | Extremely tired
test: Mum says, «We're whacked, let's go to bed.» What does whacked mean? | Hit hard | Hungry | *Extremely tired | Crazy or strange
exam: «The runners were whacked after the race.» Which meaning of whacked fits, and why? | Hit hard, because the runners were hit | *Extremely tired, because they ran a long race | Crazy, because running is strange | Brand new, because they had new shoes
